    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d110">

                <pb facs="0139" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg89"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.51/414a</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Poole</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-11-09T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 9,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>348. Please cable us text of ruble note which British are issuing at Archangel,
                    and keep us advised of method they are adopting to introduce such notes into
                    circulation, and to secure their acceptance as circulating medium and their
                    success in so doing.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
